    {
      "id": "legend2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 1906.5,
      "width": 781.2,
      "height": 351.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 576345437,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1529977524,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Not drawn, because they hold no data and sit behind every box in the pipeline lane:\n\n  Key Vault holds every secret. The container job and the Airflow VM reach it with a\n  managed identity, so there is no credential in the repository to leak or rotate.\n\n  Azure Container Registry holds the ingestion image. Every image is tagged with the\n  commit SHA, so you can answer which version of the code wrote a row.\n\n  GitHub Actions lints and tests the Python on every pull request, and on a merge to\n  main it builds the image and pushes it. No registry password lives in your repo:\n  GitHub proves which repository is running and Azure trusts that directly.\n\n  Alerting: every DAG carries a failure callback that posts the task, the reason and\n  a link to the log into Slack, so a failure at 6am reaches a person instead of\n  waiting for somebody to open Airflow.\n\n  Streamlit for pipeline health is optional, and only after the required path runs.\n  It runs as a Container App and reads dbt test results from a table the DAG writes.",
      "originalText": "Not drawn, because they hold no data and sit behind every box in the pipeline lane:\n\n  Key Vault holds every secret. The container job and the Airflow VM reach it with a\n  managed identity, so there is no credential in the repository to leak or rotate.\n\n  Azure Container Registry holds the ingestion image. Every image is tagged with the\n  commit SHA, so you can answer which version of the code wrote a row.\n\n  GitHub Actions lints and tests the Python on every pull request, and on a merge to\n  main it builds the image and pushes it. No registry password lives in your repo:\n  GitHub proves which repository is running and Azure trusts that directly.\n\n  Alerting: every DAG carries a failure callback that posts the task, the reason and\n  a link to the log into Slack, so a failure at 6am reaches a person instead of\n  waiting for somebody to open Airflow.\n\n  Streamlit for pipeline health is optional, and only after the required path runs.\n  It runs as a Container App and reads dbt test results from a table the DAG writes.",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.3,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "title3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 2377.5,
      "width": 632.4,
      "height": 39.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 37724057,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 199536895,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Architectures that are not allowed",
      "originalText": "Architectures that are not allowed",
      "fontSize": 30,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.3,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "subtitle3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 2429.5,
      "width": 1190.4,
      "height": 41.6,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 691426043,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 617414917,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Each of these works, ships, and demos. That is what makes them dangerous: nobody notices until the marks are handed out.\nThe overlap is not a mistake by any track. It is what happens when three curricula each teach the whole loop.",
      "originalText": "Each of these works, ships, and demos. That is what makes them dangerous: nobody notices until the marks are handed out.\nThe overlap is not a mistake by any track. It is what happens when three curricula each teach the whole loop.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.3,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "tldr_box",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 2507.5,
      "width": 2140,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 200137224,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 100591086,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tldr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 84,
      "y": 2535.5,
      "width": 1111.04,
      "height": 104.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 685548654,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1889595474,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Frontend lands on Next.js + TypeScript + Tailwind on Vercel; backend on Java + Spring Boot + Postgres + Flyway,\ndeployed to Render or Railway. The dangerous overlap is Backend Week 14's @Scheduled plus Week 6's API client: a\nbackend trainee can fetch Arbeitnow on a timer and write it straight to Postgres, which makes the whole data\npipeline optional. Fix with one rule: every table has exactly one writer, plus flyway.schemas=app so a backend\nmigration cannot reset your analytics schema.",
      "originalText": "Frontend lands on Next.js + TypeScript + Tailwind on Vercel; backend on Java + Spring Boot + Postgres + Flyway,\ndeployed to Render or Railway. The dangerous overlap is Backend Week 14's @Scheduled plus Week 6's API client: a\nbackend trainee can fetch Arbeitnow on a timer and write it straight to Postgres, which makes the whole data\npipeline optional. Fix with one rule: every table has exactly one writer, plus flyway.schemas=app so a backend\nmigration cannot reset your analytics schema.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.3,
